y’s labels or displays.","short_summary":"Warm up among seasonal displays and tropical plants without buying a ticket.","evidence_claim":"The City’s 2025 Manito walking-tour brochure includes Gaiser Conservatory and states that every inch of Manito Park is free and open to the public.","source_url":"https://static.spokanecity.org/documents/parks/manito/manito-park-walking-tour-brochure-2025-08-22.pdf","source_title":"A Walking Tour of Manito Park – August 2025","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":"2025-08-22","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"No admission is required; enter only during the conservatory’s posted operating hours and observe posted plant-protection rules.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"manito-joel-e-ferris-perennial-garden","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Joel E. Ferris Perennial Garden","title":"Make a Perennial Color Survey","subtitle":"A free seasonal garden walk at Manito Park","notes":"Pick a color and walk the sloping beds together, photographing or listing each different perennial bloom you find in that shade.","short_summary":"Turn a garden stroll into a collaborative search for seasonal colors.","evidence_claim":"The City’s Manito walking-tour brochure names the Joel E. Ferris Perennial Garden and says all of Manito Park is free and open to the public.","source_url":"https://static.spokanecity.org/documents/parks/manito/manito-park-walking-tour-brochure-2025-08-22.pdf","source_title":"A Walking Tour of Manito Park – August 2025","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":"2025-08-22","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Free and open to the public; remain on established paths and do not pick flowers or disturb plantings.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"manito-rose-hill","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Rose Hill","title":"Compare the Roses on Rose Hill","subtitle":"A no-ticket horticultural stop in Manito Park","notes":"Walk the beds with friends and compare bloom shape, color, and fragrance while leaving flowers and identification labels undisturbed.","short_summary":"Use the labeled rose collection as the focus of a relaxed outdoor meetup.","evidence_claim":"The City’s 2025 Manito walking-tour brochure includes Rose Hill and explicitly says every inch of Manito Park is free and open to the public.","source_url":"https://static.spokanecity.org/documents/parks/manito/manito-park-walking-tour-brochure-2025-08-22.pdf","source_title":"A Walking Tour of Manito Park – August 2025","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":"2025-08-22","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Free and open to the public; visit during park hours and keep to paths while viewing the seasonal plantings.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"riverfront-ice-age-floods-playground","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Ice Age Floods Playground","title":"Dig into Ice Age Floods","subtitle":"Free geology-themed play on Riverfront Park’s North Bank","notes":"Try the fossil dig, log-jam climber, and flood-themed features together, then connect each element to the region’s geology.","short_summary":"Mix active play with an outdoor introduction to Spokane’s Ice Age flood landscape.","evidence_claim":"The City says the North Bank amenities are free for everyone and identifies the Ice Age Floods Playground among them.","source_url":"https://my.spokanecity.org/parksrec/news/2021/05/06/riverfront-ice-age-floods-playground-north-bank-open-may-21/","source_title":"Riverfront Ice Age Floods Playground & North Bank Open May 21","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":"2021-05-06","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Free for everyone; use during posted playground hours, with the spla